                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "You've removed the non recoverable, this isn't just an \"update\".  Need some amount in the commit as to why the non recoverable (that someone else set) doesn't apply here. then this looks fine."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alex-TS-Wang",
                        "email": "alex.ts.wang@fii-foxconn.com",
                        "username": "Alex-TS-Wang"
                    },
                    "message": "After discussing with the IGS Thermal team, we will keep the non-recoverable, so the commit will remain as originally written."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't think this is resolved.  I see two concerns:\n\n1. \"Update\" is vague.  You added a new threshold.  Be clear as to what you are doing and why.\n\n2. Why does the \"IGS thermal team\" have any say on nvidia parts?  This isn't clear.  I'm guessing not everyone knows who/what IGS means, so be clear."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "(stares at IGS badge with my name on it) now this patch appears appears to just be adding a new upper warning threshold?  If that's the intent, update the commit message to that effect, and this should be fine."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
